  body: "# Revision of a DMG decision\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nRevision is described as re-examining the
    facts, law and use of discretion in a decision, with revision considered before supersession when a decision
    is challenged.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source excludes revision of First-tier and Upper Tribunal decisions.
    A newly reported change of circumstances is distinguished from revision. Application periods, any-time grounds
    and memo updates are unresolved dependencies.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 03000, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n- [DMG 03001, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n- [DMG 03009, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n- [DMG 03004, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of the 15 September
    2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance, not a consolidated
    statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an
    entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file positions. Machine
    extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve extracted text;
    no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability remain
    separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch3` PDF SHA-256: `4aebcf1988fb7d96698dce77bf88d68272a5975171decc42f58c32cfa1d42eeb`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `444fa1a240db31b94cb75c13a2f2ece7c691f15aeca0bec2dd298e2f4e08f66a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly directs consideration of revision first and supersession where revision
      is unavailable; skos:related records the distinction without an executable workflow.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch3/0002
      quote: "03001 Where a decision is challenged, the DM reconsiders it, and revises the decision if it is appropriate\n\
        to do so. Where it cannot be revised, supersession may be appropriate. The DM should always consider\nrevision
        first."
      locator: DMG 03001
  - target: term/dmg-first-tier-appeal
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source describes early revision as capable of avoiding a formal tribunal hearing, not as a
      reason to prevent a lawful appeal.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch3/0002
      quote: "03000 [See DMG Memo 13-25] The revision process allows the DM to re-examine the facts of the case,\n\
        the law used and other issues such as how discretion was applied when making a decision. Revising a\ndecision
        at an early stage, for example where an appeal is made, can avoid the need for cases to proceed\nto a formal
        FtT hearing."
      locator: DMG 03000
  - target: term/pension-credit
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The captured scope list explicitly includes SPC within the revision process; this is not a
      consolidation of current Pension Credit dispute law.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch3/0003
      quote: "03005 The revision process applies to the following\n\n\n1. all benefits including SPC, and SF maternity,
        funeral, CWPs and WFPs\n\n\n2. decisions on credits and HRP\n\n\n3. whether a JSAg is reasonable"
      locator: DMG 03005
